  "explanation": "$\\sin^{-1}(1/\\sqrt{2}) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.<br /><br />$\\cos^{-1}(1/\\sqrt{2}) = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.<br /><br />Also $\\tan^{-1}(1/\\sqrt{2}) + \\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt{2}) = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.<br /><br />Since $\\cot^{-1}(1/\\sqrt{2}) = \\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt{2})$.<br /><br />Thus $\\tan^{-1}(1/\\sqrt{2}) + \\cot^{-1}(1/\\sqrt{2}) = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.<br /><br />Adding all values<br /><br />$\\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\pi$.<br /><br />Therefore $f\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) = \\pi$.",
